<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PermissionSet xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        🔴 THIS SET WILL NOT DEPLOY UNTIL "SharePoint_Credential" EXISTS IN THE ORG.
        `externalCredentialPrincipalAccesses.externalCredentialPrincipal` below references
        "SharePoint_Credential-SharePoint_Principal" by name. Per the admin-agent decision recorded
        in ARCHITECTURE.md §3.4, the `SharePoint_Credential` External Credential is deliberately NOT
        shipped as metadata in this repo (the OAuth 2.0 / client-credentials ExternalCredential XML
        shape could not be confirmed via salesforce-api-context MCP at API 67.0, and the in-repo
        precedent, OpenAI_Credential, is authenticationProtocol "Custom" — a different protocol with
        a different parameter shape that does not transfer). It must be created BY HAND in Setup
        first (Auth. Protocol = OAuth 2.0, Flow = Client Credentials with Client Secret, one Named
        Principal literally named "SharePoint_Principal"). Deploy this permission set (and
        SharePoint.namedCredential-meta.xml) only after that manual step is done.

        UserExternalCredential object read is REQUIRED TO USE ANY Named Credential at all —
        precedent: Broker_Protection_Access.permissionset-meta.xml carries the identical grant with
        the identical justification ("without object read on UserExternalCredential the callout
        throws before sending", found via debug log 2026-08-01 on this same org). Do not omit it.

        No fieldPermissions, no classAccesses — there is no Apex in this request (design-requirements-
        sharepoint-credentials.md §4). Keeping this file at zero field permissions also means the
        REPLACE-not-merge permission-set-deploy hazard documented in ARCHITECTURE.md §2 (Standards)
        has nothing to destroy on a future redeploy of this file.
    -->
    <description>Grants External Credential Principal Access to SharePoint_Credential (Microsoft Graph OAuth) plus UserExternalCredential read, required to invoke the SharePoint Named Credential. See ARCHITECTURE.md §3.4.</description>
    <externalCredentialPrincipalAccesses>
        <enabled>true</enabled>
        <externalCredentialPrincipal>SharePoint_Credential-SharePoint_Principal</externalCredentialPrincipal>
    </externalCredentialPrincipalAccesses>
    <hasActivationRequired>false</hasActivationRequired>
    <label>SharePoint Integration Access</label>
    <objectPermissions>
        <allowCreate>false</allowCreate>
        <allowDelete>false</allowDelete>
        <allowEdit>false</allowEdit>
        <allowRead>true</allowRead>
        <modifyAllRecords>false</modifyAllRecords>
        <object>UserExternalCredential</object>
        <viewAllRecords>false</viewAllRecords>
    </objectPermissions>
</PermissionSet>
